# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node / Worker
node_modules/
.wrangler/
dist/

# Fetched data never belongs in the repository. Note this is deliberately NOT
# "data/": data/stations.json is the station registry that both TypeScript and
# Python read, and it must be committed. A blanket "data/" ignore meant the
# registry was never added, the Worker kept working because esbuild inlines
# the import at build time, and only CI noticed.
data/*.jsonl
data/latest.json
data/health.json

# Secrets. Local values live in .env (Python fetchers) and .dev.vars (the
# Worker under `npm run dev`); .env.example, committed, lists the names. This
# repository is public. Two checks back the ignore rules up: .githooks/
# pre-commit refuses secrets files, credential-shaped strings and the values in
# .env and .dev.vars (enable once per clone with
# `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`), and CI scans every push for the same
# shapes, from scripts/secret-patterns.txt. The live values are GitHub Actions
# secrets and a Cloudflare Worker secret, never files here.
*.local.md
.cdsapirc
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.venv/
.npm-cache/
.git-creds
.git-credentials

# The design and research documents stay local: this repository is public and
# they contain the commercial strategy. docs/ carries what the build needs.
*.docx

.DS_Store

# Development seed, regenerated from a real CAMS download; never committed.
dev-seed.sql

# Generated SQL from the fetchers; applied, never committed.
sql/
*.grib
# cfgrib writes a sibling index beside each download.
*.grib.*.idx
.cache/

# Candidate logo artwork, kept locally while one is chosen.
Logo options/
